{%- doc -%}
  Echoes a pasted SVG with its `<style>` blocks removed.

  A `<style>` element inside an inlined SVG is **not** scoped to that SVG: once the markup is in
  the document, the browser treats it as a document stylesheet like any other. Illustrator exports
  routinely ship rules such as `path, rect { fill: #F5F4EA; }`, which then repaint every icon on
  the page - the header cart and account icons included.

  Inline `style` attributes on the shapes are left alone: those only affect their own element, and
  they are what keeps these logos looking right once the block is gone.

  @param {string} svg - The pasted SVG markup.

  @example
  {% render 'svg-without-styles', svg: block.settings.logo_svg %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign chunks = svg | split: '<style'
  assign output = chunks[0]

  for chunk in chunks offset: 1
    assign tail = chunk | split: '</style>'

    # No closing tag means the markup is malformed; dropping the remainder is safer than echoing
    # a stylesheet the browser would apply to the whole page.
    if tail.size > 1
      for piece in tail offset: 1
        assign output = output | append: piece
      endfor
    endif
  endfor

  echo output
-%}
